 "preferred_name": "Async/await",
 "kind": "method",
 "definition": "A programming pattern, supported by syntax in languages such as C#, JavaScript and Python, that lets asynchronous operations be written in code that reads like sequential steps.",
 "description": {
  "text": "A syntax feature in many programming languages that lets an asynchronous, non-blocking function be written like an ordinary synchronous one. It is related to coroutines and lets a program run other code while waiting on long operations.",
